  "question": {
    "text": "The binding energy per nucleon of deuteron (<math><mmultiscripts><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></math>and helium nucleus (<math><mmultiscripts><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></math>is 1.1 MeV and 7 MeV respectively. If two deuteron nuclei react to form a single helium nucleus, then the energy released is",
    "image": null
  },
